`forwardRef` is deprecated. Pass `ref` directly as a prop to function components.

<details><summary><b>Before / After Example</b></summary>

```typescript
// ❌ BEFORE (React 18/19 wrapper)
const MyButton = forwardRef((props, ref) => {
  return <button ref={ref} {...props} />;
});

// ✅ AFTER (React 19/20 ref prop)
function MyButton({ ref, ...props }: { ref?: React.Ref<HTMLButtonElement> }) {
  return <button ref={ref} {...props} />;
}
```
</details>

`defaultProps` on function components is removed in React 20. Use ES6 default parameter syntax.

<details><summary><b>Before / After Example</b></summary>

```typescript
// ❌ BEFORE
function Badge({ color }: { color?: string }) {
  return <span className={color} />;
}
Badge.defaultProps = { color: 'blue' };

// ✅ AFTER
function Badge({ color = 'blue' }: { color?: string }) {
  return <span className={color} />;
}
```
</details>

Legacy Context API (`contextTypes`) is removed in React 20. Migrate to `React.createContext()`.

<details><summary><b>Before / After Example</b></summary>

```typescript
// ❌ BEFORE (Legacy Context)
class Child extends React.Component {
  static contextTypes = { theme: PropTypes.string };
}

// ✅ AFTER (Modern Context)
const ThemeContext = React.createContext('light');
function Child() {
  const theme = use(ThemeContext);
  return <div className={theme} />;
}
```
</details>

`react-dom/test-utils` has been removed in React 20. Use `@testing-library/react`.

<details><summary><b>Before / After Example</b></summary>

```typescript
// ❌ BEFORE
import { act } from 'react-dom/test-utils';

// ✅ AFTER
import { act } from 'react';
// or
import { render, screen } from '@testing-library/react';
```
</details>
